# Documentation actualization (cxado core)

Documentation is part of the agent chain ([core-workflow-chain.mdc](core-workflow-chain.mdc)) — its **Document** step, after critic APPROVE and merge, is this checklist.

## Generic checklist

| Artifact | When to update |
|----------|----------------|
| Master / phase plans | Phase `done`, merge SHA |
| README.md | User-facing behavior, quick start, tests |
| AGENTS.md | Workflow or verify checklist changes |
| Project architecture docs | API, security, or runtime flow changes |

Project overlay lists repo-specific paths.

## Phase plan template

```markdown
## Scope
## Out of scope
## Files
## Acceptance (commands)
## Docs to touch on merge
```

## Reasoning quality

- Constraint-first: state architecture bans before coding.
- Few-shot: link one good prior phase as pattern.
- Counterfactual: «What would fail in CI?» — list exact commands.
